<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb beef imports fall 20.2 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Feb beef imports fall 20.2 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's beef imports in February totalled 39,313 tonnes, down by 20.2 percent against a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Friday showed.</p>
<p>Details were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    Feb 97	 Jan 97     Feb 96</p>
<p> Total	    39,313	 40,514     49,272</p>
<p> Refrigerated   26,201	 20,977     27,723</p>
<p> Frozen	   13,112	 19,537     15,734</p>
<p>Major suppliers of refrigerated beef (in tonnes):</p>
<p>  Australia     15,905	 11,684     16,426</p>
<p>  U.S.	     9,405	  8,651     10,388</p>
<p>Major suppliers of frozen beef (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    Feb 97	 Jan 97	Feb 96</p>
<p> U.S.		6,665	  9,700	8,694</p>
<p> Australia	 4,764	  7,832	5,814</p>
<p>Cumulative imports of refrigerated beef in the first two months of 1997 were 47,177 tonnes against 51,802 tonnes a year earlier.</p>
<p>Frozen beef imports in the January-February period of this year were 32,649 tonnes against 40,929 tonnes in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
</text>
